261
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:50,720
And don't forget, my name is Heraclesin!

262
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:54,040
Huh? Usoppun?

263
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,400
Where did you go?

264
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:02,620
Oh, no!

265
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:06,195
The sea creature in has just
crawled onto the Island!

266
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,330
Usoppun!

267
00:16:07,413 --> 00:16:08,560
You're in danger!

268
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:16,497
The sweet flavors and intoxicating aromas
that emanate from the Bowen Islands?

269
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,680
attract a plethora of
giant insects and birds.

270
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:23,920
Even sea kings and other aquatic
animals visit from time to time.

271
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,220
It's your sea hippo.

272
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,456
Now's not the time to stop and stare.

273
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:34,717
The wonderful smells lead
them deeper onto the island.

274
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:38,220
There, they find ever
more tempting flavors.

275
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,860
But while it's easy to enter the island,

276
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,640
it's much harder to leave.

277
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:53,500
Another one!

278
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:55,400
Try my exploding star!

279
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:01,204
I'm getting out of here
no matter what it takes!

280
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:03,200
Don't you dare get on my way!

281
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:10,137
The islands are gonna move again!

282
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:11,500
Wait, do what now?

283
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:16,760
Stop in!

284
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,740
Grab a tree and hang on!

285
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,820
How often does this happen?

286
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:22,840
Every time it needs to feed!

287
00:17:28,940 --> 00:17:32,860
The so-called Bowen Islands are
not at all what they appear.

288
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,237
The flower-shaped island is actually an

289
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:51,820
island-sized flower known
as the Stomach Berry

290
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,020
Oh, supper!

291
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,400
What has gotten into you?

292
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:12,517
Ever since the news coup brought that
paper, you've been acting like a maniac.

293
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:13,541
What did it say?

294
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,760
I can't be here!

295
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,820
I have to go!

296
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:24,526
I've wasted enough time
on this stupid island!

297
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,820
Luffy, he lost his brother in the war!

298
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:39,940
And now, he doesn't know where
we are or if we're alive!

299
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:01,440
Luffy wouldn't let me suffer like that!

300
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:03,420
I'm his friend!

301
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:05,720
I need to be there for him!

302
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,400
I'm sorry, Luffy!

303
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:20,180
We not long ago make friends.

304
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,211
Raccoon really leave now?

305
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:24,950
Yeah.

306
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:28,777
As soon as I read that newspaper and found
out what my friend's been going through,

307
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:31,566
I realized I couldn't
stick around any longer.

308
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:35,300
I had just met Luffy's
brother in Alabasta.

309
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:38,076
I can't believe what happened to him.

310
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,860
I'm worried about Luffy.

311
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:43,399
What if he needs medical attention?

312
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:47,200
He always pushes himself
way too hard. Good friend.

313
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:51,877
Anyway, it's good to see you and the
birds are getting along better now.

314
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:56,377
Understanding only happened because brave
raccoon friend risking life to do talking.

315
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:57,290
Aww.

316
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:01,791
You guys remember not to pick
fights with the humans, okay?

317
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:04,428
They're not gonna hurt you.

318
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:08,277
They just want you to let them pick
the plants that grow on that tree.

319
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:12,000
Raccoon, speaking truth, we
no fight you are taking eggs.

320
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:16,137
We not same as bad humans that stealing
your treasure and chase you away.

321
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:17,560
We're your friends!

322
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:19,940
Oh, by the way,

323
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:21,637
I was really impressed with that medicine

324
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,897
you guys gave me when
I got injured before.

325
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:24,980
It's great stuff.

326
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:27,400
See, I'm better already. Right.

327
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:31,856
We using special medicine recipe we
passing down over many generations.

328
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,000
To tell you the truth,

329
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:39,097
I wish I could stay here with you guys
and study those plants for a while.

330
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:43,697
I'm sure there's still a lot I could learn,
but the timing's kind of bad right now.

331
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,177
Come back soon, okay?

332
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:46,140
Not right.

333
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:48,478
You're always welcome here, Raccoon.

334
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:51,670
Really?

335
00:20:51,753 --> 00:20:53,100
That makes me so happy.

336
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:57,054
After my friends and I find each other,

337
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:59,817
I'll tell them all about
this amazing place I found.

338
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:03,640
And I promise, when I can,
I'll come back and visit, okay?

339
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:05,650
Take.

340
00:21:05,733 --> 00:21:06,563
Journey long.

341
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:09,280
Maybe get hungry. Oh, wow. Thanks.

342
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:10,520
See Raccoon soon.

343
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:14,130
Hey!

344
00:21:14,213 --> 00:21:15,640
I love cotton candy!

345
00:21:17,020 --> 00:21:18,300
So long, everybody!

346
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:20,020
Be nice to each other!

347
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,140
Goodbye, raccoon!

348
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,320
You travel soon!

349
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,637
Now that I've got a yummy lunch
and all the cotton candy I can eat,

350
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:30,191
I'm ready to head for the
meeting spot so I can help Luffy!

351
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:31,530
Wait!

352
00:21:31,613 --> 00:21:33,809
I just realized I don't
have a pirate ship!

353
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:35,660
Woohoo! Lucky me!

354
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:38,517
Why didn't I think of
this in the first place?

355
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,365
I'll be there in no time flat.

356
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:42,160
You're so fast, Mr. Bird.

357
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:46,680
Hey, News Koo, I'll take one of those.

358
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,875
I can read this while I have my lunch.

359
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:54,899
They should have some new
info about the war by now.

360
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:00,810
What?

361
00:22:00,893 --> 00:22:01,723
That's crazy!

362
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:04,730
No way.

363
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:05,997
I don't believe it.

364
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:07,140
Luffy!

365
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:08,680
What's going on?

366
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:17,300
This is Gloom Island on the Grand Line,
home to the ruins of the Monkey Kingdom.

367
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:21,120
An old castle remains
from the long-dead empire.

368
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:25,380
Despite its age, a well-known
figure has made the castle his home.

369
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,060
Why did Mario have to get himself killed?

370
00:22:39,620 --> 00:22:40,900
You're being a pest.

371
00:22:41,020 --> 00:22:42,760
Go and cry somewhere else.

372
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:45,457
How can you be so heartless
when I'm grieving?

373
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:47,497
Show some compassion, you big Moon!

374
00:22:47,580 --> 00:22:49,521
Do you have anything kind to say?

375
00:22:49,820 --> 00:22:50,920
Offer me a tissue!

376
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:52,160
I'm your guest!

377
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:53,948
Your manners are appalling!

378
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,720
I never invited you.

379
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:59,705
The two of you showed up and
started living here without asking.

380
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:04,360
Furthermore, this article
is not credible. What?

381
00:23:04,780 --> 00:23:07,486
But does that mean Moria
could still be alive?

382
00:23:07,660 --> 00:23:08,542
He made it out?

383
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:11,200
A good question, now you ask.

384
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:14,680
If he died, then I didn't see it.

385
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:19,240
Although, if he did escape, then I
didn't see that either, I'm afraid.

386
00:23:19,780 --> 00:23:24,486
But you think he might have survived and
they're lying about it for some reason?

387
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,590
Honey?

388
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:30,650
Kitty!

389
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:41,477
You can't fix that with your spits!

390
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:44,325
Who even taught you that
garbage, your grandma?

391
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:49,530
Bastards.

392
00:23:49,613 --> 00:23:52,027
They may be stupid, but
damn, they're strong.

393
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:55,519
At this rate, I'm never
going to make it to the sea.

394
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:05,870
Hawkeye.

395
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:11,517
It's been quite a while since you left the
castle, yet you've only made it this far.

396
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:12,430
Pity.

397
00:24:12,513 --> 00:24:16,460
And the boat I offered you, it
seems it's not seaworthy now.

398
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:19,000
Shut up. It's fine.

399
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:21,597
We could just hold on to a
few planks and swim there.

400
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:23,957
I'm not one to give up
that easily, all right?

401
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:28,280
Your sentiment is admirable,
but you can't defeat them.

402
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:33,780
They're called humandrills, baboons that
develop by imitating human behavior.

403
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:35,550
Humandrills?

404
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:40,617
Had they grown up among peace-loving humans,
they would have turned out differently.

405
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:42,360
But not on this island.

406
00:24:43,740 --> 00:24:47,360
Up until seven years ago, this
was the site of a great war.

407
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:54,380
When I first came here to live, the entire
island still smelled of blood and smoke.

408
00:24:54,900 --> 00:24:57,488
Everywhere, dead bodies
littered the ground.

409
00:24:58,280 --> 00:24:59,880
As the battles raged on,

410
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:03,277
these baboons watched the violence
between the humans unfold.

411
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:06,217
In time, they learned how to
use human weapons and armor,

412
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:08,182
becoming warriors of the forest.

413
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:12,842
Humans can defeat ordinary animals
by using weapons and intellect.

414
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:16,100
But what happens when
animals don weapons as well?

415
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:20,717
As you can see, they make formidable
opponents for an arrogant young man.

416
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:22,035
You talking about me?

417
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:23,240
Well, who else?

418
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:26,097
Now, let's leave. It's late.

419
00:25:26,180 --> 00:25:29,240
that your mandrels won't
set foot near the castle.

420
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:33,100
Yeah, you got no right
telling me what to do.

421
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:36,000
I've got to make it to the sea.

422
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:37,640
Of course.

423
00:25:38,940 --> 00:25:40,140
Do as you like.

424
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:45,580
I don't care if they're
forest warriors or monkeys.

425
00:25:45,720 --> 00:25:48,896
I've already wasted enough
time stranded in this dump.

426
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:58,886
Meanwhile, on the floating
island of Weatheria,

427
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:04,720
the world's foremost meteorologists are
busy coping with a most unruly guest.

428
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:12,037
I'll give back what I borrowed!

429
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:14,649
Just let me out of this
stupid bubble jail!

430
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:16,590
Horridus!

431
00:26:16,673 --> 00:26:18,497
Get Horridus, and he'll sort this out!

432
00:26:18,580 --> 00:26:19,462
Gritty, please!

433
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:23,320
We're old and you're scary!

434
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:25,637
Who knows what kind of
trap you're plotting?

435
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:27,360
This is a place of law.

436
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:29,257
You'll be punished for your crimes.

437
00:26:29,340 --> 00:26:32,222
Yes, what if we shocked
her or drowned her a bit?

438
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:34,460
Which better befits a thief?

439
00:26:36,060 --> 00:26:37,884
Ugh, you guys got it all wrong.

440
00:26:38,320 --> 00:26:41,000
Please, let me out, at
least give me a trial.

441
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,540
No way, Missy!

442
00:26:47,980 --> 00:26:49,860
Oh, hello, Horidot.

443
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,480
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

444
00:26:56,340 --> 00:26:58,540
Well, well, what a pickle.

445
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,880
Hey, young lady. Hey yourself.

446
00:27:01,220 --> 00:27:02,400
Another outburst.

447
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:05,444
You just weren't made to
take it easy, were you?

448
00:27:05,820 --> 00:27:07,140
But never fear.

449
00:27:07,420 --> 00:27:09,157
You remember this fellow, right?

450
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:10,737
Here, I'll show you a trick.

451
00:27:10,820 --> 00:27:13,620
Take your tightly tied wind knots like so.

452
00:27:17,860 --> 00:27:18,900
Hurrah, snow!

453
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:24,921
I was counting on you to help me!

454
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:26,178
Get me out of here!

455
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:27,437
I'm in a rush, all right?

456
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:28,350
Are you okay?

457
00:27:28,760 --> 00:27:30,360
Hard enough speak to us!

458
00:27:30,460 --> 00:27:31,872
Tell us you're not dead!

459
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:34,980
Uh, yes or no.

460
00:27:35,300 --> 00:27:36,340
I mean, maybe.

461
00:27:36,660 --> 00:27:40,920
She hit that kind and gentle
man! What a beast! Doctor!

462
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:42,852
Someone call the doctor!

463
00:27:47,060 --> 00:27:48,400
That's most curious.

464
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:52,217
So she stole an armful of weather
balls in our research notes,

465
00:27:52,300 --> 00:27:53,957
which then tried to make a break for it?

466
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:55,040
See for yourself.

467
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,336
It's all right here.

468
00:27:57,720 --> 00:27:58,600
Young lady.

469
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:00,297
I'm a pirate.

470
00:28:00,380 --> 00:28:01,556
What did you expect?

471
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:03,699
What's wrong with the little theft?

472
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:06,657
Got to make a living somehow, don't I?

473
00:28:06,740 --> 00:28:09,700
Simply reprehensible,
such an awful human being.

474
00:28:10,040 --> 00:28:11,797
We have no villain in our midst.

475
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:13,115
Whatever shall we do?

476
00:28:14,880 --> 00:28:16,020
Just let me go.

477
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:19,597
You guys don't want me here,
and I don't want to be here.

478
00:28:19,680 --> 00:28:21,337
You got back everything I stole.

479
00:28:21,420 --> 00:28:22,891
What does it even matter?

480
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:26,037
Would you stop flipping out for
five seconds and listen to me?

481
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,137
I'm in a hurry here!

482
00:28:27,220 --> 00:28:28,279
This is important!

483
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,260
Don't get too close!

484
00:28:30,460 --> 00:28:32,260
It's terribly violent!

485
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:37,231
All right, I'm listening.

486
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,230
Let's talk.

487
00:28:38,820 --> 00:28:43,300
Though I should tell you, stealing a
balloon was both foolish and dangerous.

488
00:28:43,700 --> 00:28:45,935
You need proper training to pilot one.

489
00:28:46,020 --> 00:28:47,608
You could have easily died.

490
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:51,500
Read the front page.

491
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:54,100
The paper, eh?

492
00:28:55,620 --> 00:28:58,561
You see that article about
the pirate named Luffy?

493
00:28:58,660 --> 00:29:01,140
He's the captain of our ship. Is he?

494
00:29:02,820 --> 00:29:04,960
Oh, I've seen that fellow before.

495
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:06,711
The boy's a real upstart.

496
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:09,197
Caused quite the ruckus
in Marineford, they say.

497
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:11,537
He's famous for that
Straw Hat that he wears.

498
00:29:11,620 --> 00:29:13,877
Our crew has been
separated for a while now,

499
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,977
so he doesn't even know
if we're alive or dead.

500
00:29:16,060 --> 00:29:19,840
I had no idea what he was going
through until I read that paper.

501
00:29:22,820 --> 00:29:24,897
I've been taking it easy all this time,

502
00:29:24,980 --> 00:29:27,686
while he was down there
fighting for his life.

503
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:36,324
He saw his brother killed
right before his eyes.

504
00:29:36,760 --> 00:29:38,040
I didn't even know.

505
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:40,360
I couldn't do anything.

506
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,800
Now he's waiting for me.

507
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:47,340
and for the rest of the crew, I'm sure.

508
00:29:49,660 --> 00:29:52,366
Luffy is strong, but
this is too much to bear.

509
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:57,477
I want to be there for him.

510
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:58,900
I want to help him.

511
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:07,080
Hey, hey, don't cry. You'll be okay.

512
00:30:07,820 --> 00:30:09,420
Hurry up and let her out.

513
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:10,877
We're the real villains.

514
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:11,790
Look at us.

515
00:30:11,873 --> 00:30:15,114
Oh, abducting an innocent
young girl and making her cry!

516
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:16,197
Give Harados the key!

517
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:17,110
Quickly now!

518
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:19,120
We're sorry, young lady.

519
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:20,660
